-- title:
--   Pole chart of X_H(q²M') regular at cusp ∞, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H = \mathrm{levelH}\ q\ M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of the modular $j$-function, and let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$. Write $A_\infty = \mathrm{chartAlgInf}\ A\ K\ j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, and let $\mathfrak n \subseteq A_\infty$ be a prime ideal consisting exactly of those $b$ whose Laurent coefficient in degree $0$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$. Then for any localisation $B_{\mathfrak m}$ of $A_\infty$ at $\mathfrak n$: $B_{\mathfrak m}$ is a regular local ring, its Krull dimension is $2$, the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak n$ equals the ideal generated by the images of $\varpi$ and of $j^{-1}$ (the element $\mathrm{jInvChartInf}\ A\ K\ j$), and the quotient of $B_{\mathfrak m}$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ is again a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the regularity statement at the $\mathsf q$-adic cusp $\infty$ on the pole chart of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $H = \ker((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times)$, in the case $q = 3$ (the companion to the case $q \ge 5$), exhibiting $(\varpi, 1/j)$ as a regular system of parameters and the special fibre as regular there. It feeds the analysis of the fibre of the model along the Igusa leg of the semistable covering.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty_xH_of_eq_three.lean

